{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"printed-woeful-queenant","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n\nCriterion DISCOVERY and prompt RESOLUTION resolve their repo root by different rules, and nothing\ndetects when the two disagree.\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/criteria/overlay.py:77-88` (`_resolve_repo_root`) falls back to `config.repo_root()`\n  when passed `None`, so a project criterion is ACTIVATED from the ambient checkout.\n- `src/rebar/llm/prompting/prompts.py:213-221` (`get_prompt`) has no fallback: it gates the project\n  override lookup on `if repo_root:`, so a `None` root silently skips `.rebar/prompts/` and falls\n  through to `PromptNotFound` at :226.\n\n`_resolve_repo_root`'s own docstring asserts it returns \"the same root `get_prompt` resolves\n`.rebar/prompts/` overrides against\". That is FALSE. The symmetry it claims has never existed, so\nthis is an unenforced invariant, not a deliberate split.\n\nBug 2ea4 (closed duplicate) was one live instance: criterion activated from cwd, prompt looked up\nwith `repo_root=None`, hard `LLMError`. Commit `b3953a0da` (ticket 22f5) repaired that one call path\nby computing `execution_repo_root = cfg.repo_path` in `llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py:698` and passing\nit to both stages. Nothing PREVENTS the next caller from reintroducing the split.\n\nTwo distinct defects remain:\n\n1. **No detection.** Discovery and resolution take independent `repo_root: str | None` parameters at\n   two different depths. A caller can supply different roots, or one and not the other, and the\n   mismatch is invisible until it surfaces as an unrelated-looking error.\n2. **The error is inaccurate and not remediable.** `PromptNotFound` reports\n   `unknown prompt '<id>'; known built-ins: [...]`. For a client project whose `.rebar/prompts/<id>.md`\n   exists and is correct, this message is actively misleading: the prompt is not unknown, it was\n   never searched for. The message names neither the effective root nor the path that was checked, so\n   a client project cannot act on it.\n\n## Decision (made by the operator; do not re-litigate)\n\nFail loudly, with an accurate error a client project can remediate. Specifically:\n\n- Do NOT give `get_prompt` the ambient `config.repo_root()` fallback. Attested gate runs deliberately\n  re-root onto a pinned snapshot (`b3953a0da`); an ambient fallback would load project prompts from the\n  developer's working tree while reviewing pinned content and SUCCEED. A silently-wrong review is worse\n  than a hard failure.\n- Do NOT remove discovery's fallback. That would silently stop activating project criteria for callers\n  passing `None` — under-enforcement, quieter and worse than the current loud error.\n- Therefore: keep the two fallback rules as they are, and add an explicit check at the seam that the\n  root used for discovery is the root used for resolution, failing loudly when they differ.\n\n## Approach\n\nResolve the root once per run at the entry point and thread one value, rather than resolving it twice\nat two depths. Where discovery and resolution meet, verify they agree and raise a descriptive error if\nnot. Rewrite the not-found error so it distinguishes the three cases and names the remedy:\n\n- a project root WAS supplied and `.rebar/prompts/<id>.md` is absent — name the exact path searched;\n- NO root was supplied, so project prompts were not searched at all — say so explicitly, rather than\n  claiming the id is unknown;\n- the id is genuinely not a packaged prompt and no project root could supply it — the current message.\n\n`get_prompt(repo_root=None)` must KEEP meaning \"packaged prompts only\" and must remain legal: 23 test\ncall sites and the finalizer at `llm/workflow/completion_recovery.py:488` depend on it, and packaged\nprompts must resolve with no checkout at all (library use).\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/prompting/prompts.py` — the `if repo_root:` guard and the `PromptNotFound` message.\n- `src/rebar/llm/criteria/overlay.py` — the seam check; correct the false docstring at :79-81.\n- `src/rebar/llm/code_review/batch_runner.py:113-141` — the validation site that surfaces the error.\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/registry.py:259,308,334,519` — aliases `_resolve_repo_root` and calls it at\n  three sites, so plan-review shares this seam and must be covered, not just code-review.\n\n## Testing\n\n- A project criterion activated from a root whose `.rebar/prompts/<id>.md` EXISTS resolves that prompt\n  (client-project override path works end to end).\n- A packaged prompt resolves with `repo_root=None` (unchanged; pin the existing contract).\n- Discovery root != resolution root raises a descriptive error naming both roots, not `PromptNotFound`.\n- A missing project prompt under a supplied root produces a message naming the exact path searched.\n- Both gates covered: code-review AND plan-review.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Discovery and resolution disagreeing on the repo root fails loudly with an error naming both\n      roots; verified by a unit test that supplies mismatched roots.\n- [ ] The not-found error distinguishes \"no root supplied, project prompts not searched\" from\n      \"root supplied, path absent\" and names the searched path; verified by tests on both branches.\n- [ ] A client project's `.rebar/prompts/<id>.md` override resolves for an activated project criterion\n      in both the code-review and plan-review gates; verified by a test per gate.\n- [ ] `get_prompt(repo_root=None)` still resolves packaged prompts; existing 23 test call sites and\n      completion_recovery.py:488 keep passing.\n- [ ] The false symmetry claim in overlay.py's `_resolve_repo_root` docstring is corrected.\n- [ ] make lint, make typecheck, and the default suite exit zero.","id":"dc05-5a87-3f5c-4f99","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Prompt resolution and criterion discovery can use different repo roots; the resulting error is inaccurate and not remediable by a client project"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785516979759762001,"uuid":"833def87-764e-4d17-823b-cad93b8fe78a"}